From: AX6 EDMA correctness audit
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] edma_v1: save DMA handle for TX completion unmap

The TX completion path reconstructs the DMA address via virt_to_phys()
instead of using the handle returned by dma_map_single(). The Linux
DMA API requires dma_unmap_single() to be called with the SAME handle
that dma_map_single() returned.

On IPQ807x with identity-mapped DMA this may work by coincidence, but
it is not portable and breaks under IOMMU or swiotlb.

Save the DMA handle and mapped length in each TX store entry, and use
them in the completion path. Also clear the entry after unmap to
prevent double-unmap.

Fixes F2 from AX6 cross-audit 2026-07-26.
⚠ PATCH NEEDS BUILD-TREE VERIFICATION: the TX store entry structure
  (tx_skb_store or equivalent) must be extended with dma_handle and
  dma_len fields. Verify the structure layout against QSDK source.

--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_data_plane.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_data_plane.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ struct edma_tx_store_entry {
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
+	dma_addr_t dma_handle;
+	size_t dma_len;
 };

@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static int edma_tx_packet(struct sk_buff
 	preheader = edma_get_preheader_len();
 	dma = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, skb_headlen(skb) + preheader,
 			     DMA_TO_DEVICE);
 	if (dma_mapping_error(dev, dma))
 		goto drop;

+	store_entry->dma_handle = dma;
+	store_entry->dma_len    = skb_headlen(skb) + preheader;
+
 	/* ... TX descriptor programming ... */

@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static int edma_tx_completion(struct edm
 	store_idx = completion->store_index;
 	store_entry = &tx_skb_store[store_idx];

-	dma_addr = virt_to_phys(store_entry->skb->data);
-	dma_unmap_single(dev, dma_addr, skb_headlen(store_entry->skb) + preheader,
-			 DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+	dma_unmap_single(dev, store_entry->dma_handle, store_entry->dma_len,
+			 DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+	store_entry->dma_handle = 0;
+	store_entry->dma_len = 0;

 	dev_kfree_skb_any(store_entry->skb);
+	store_entry->skb = NULL;
